1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,150
The last team to win three NBA titles in a row?

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:05,330
The Los Angeles Lakers.

3
00:00:05,380 --> 00:00:08,590
2000. 2001. 2002.

4
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:11,390
Shaq and Kobe. Three straight rings.

5
00:00:11,440 --> 00:00:15,050
In 2001, they went 15 and 1 in the playoffs.

6
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:17,610
One loss — the whole postseason.

7
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:19,910
Since then? 24 years…

8
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:21,890
and nobody has done it again.

9
00:00:21,940 --> 00:00:24,410
Now, for the first time since 2018,

10
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:26,150
there’s no LeBron in LA.

11
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:27,830
This is Luka’s team.

12
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:30,610
And it’s working. 14 and 3.

13
00:00:30,660 --> 00:00:31,830
First in the West.

14
00:00:31,880 --> 00:00:34,210
Luka is dropping 37 a night.

15
00:00:34,260 --> 00:00:35,550
Austin Reaves is back.

16
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:37,750
Walker Kessler is owning the paint.

17
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:39,590
But the road is brutal.

18
00:00:39,640 --> 00:00:41,670
Wemby’s Spurs — the title favorites.

19
00:00:41,720 --> 00:00:43,710
The Knicks — the defending champs.

20
00:00:43,760 --> 00:00:46,550
And LeBron, now in Philly, standing in the way.

21
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:47,990
Plus their own problems:

22
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:50,510
thin at forward, and no real backup center.

23
00:00:50,560 --> 00:00:52,770
Vegas? About 25 to 1.

24
00:00:52,820 --> 00:00:55,770
So… can Luka start the next Lakers dynasty?

25
00:00:55,820 --> 00:00:58,110
One ring. Then two. Then three.

26
00:00:58,160 --> 00:00:59,950
Drop your pick in the comments.

